CLUB: SPLIT 3/8 BAVARIAN CONTEST CLUB, 3/8 SOUTHERN CALIFORNIA CONTEST CLUB, 1/8 KANSAS CITY CONTEST CLUB, 1/8 YANKEE CLIPPER CONTEST CLUB
CREATED-BY: Win-Test 4.57.0
SOAPBOX: Well, that was a thrilling weekend! A big thanks to Alex, KH6YY, and Tracy, KH6CAT, for inviting us
SOAPBOX: into their slice of paradise, for their hospitality and use of such a fine station. Jim, N6TJ, put
SOAPBOX: together the crew.
SOAPBOX: 160=K1ZM, Jeff
SOAPBOX: 80=N6TJ, Jim
SOAPBOX: 40=NH7T, John
SOAPBOX: 20=N5OT, Mark
SOAPBOX: 15=N6AA, Dick
SOAPBOX: 10=N6AN, David
SOAPBOX: Kimo, KH7U, and Stuart, NH6N, provided operator relief and lots of problem solving. Kudos to Bob,
SOAPBOX: N6TV, for all of the software related work including antenna switching, radio setup and logging
SOAPBOX: software.
SOAPBOX: N6TJ, NH7T and KH7U are regulars here, N5OT returned after ~30 years, N6AN was here last year.
SOAPBOX: Jeff enjoyed his first visit. Dick, as is well known, has been everywhere at least once.
SOAPBOX: Everyone earned their BIC honors, with special mention to N5OT/NH6N on 20 where QSOs were logged
SOAPBOX: during all but three hours. Also of note, 20 exceeded last year's result with more QSOs/(highest
SOAPBOX: hour rate), zones and countries. Jim raised last year's bar in similar fashion. Dick and Jeff
SOAPBOX: surpassed 2024 QSO totals. John saw 40 give fewer Qs, but more mults. Dick upped the QSO total on
SOAPBOX: 15 with a reduction in mults. 10 was a different band this year, despite some good rates, and
SOAPBOX: finished down 100 Qs, 3 zones and 38 countries. Europe, with a few exceptions was a reach too
SOAPBOX: far. Despite the solar instability, multiplier bells rang frequently as DX called in or heard us
SOAPBOX: calling them. Our final result exceeded last year's total despite weaker conditions.
SOAPBOX: Tracy treated us to the traditional post contest hamburger lunch. Yum!
SOAPBOX: Thanks to the travelers who put multipliers, exotic and common, on the air. And congratulations
SOAPBOX: to all the operators who turned on their radios, those setting new records and those who got on
SOAPBOX: to make a few Qs.
SOAPBOX: 73, David N6AN
SOAPBOX: P.S. It was an honor and thrill for Mark and me to operate with two mentors and heroes from our
SOAPBOX: formative years. Thank you, Dick and Jim!
